@format 1
@id media-loading.common.backend-load
@title Backend load
@section Media loading
@area Common
@entry backend-start
@summary Trace LMediaLoadAsync through normalization, request ownership, source validation, ffprobe execution, successful-read ownership checks, and raised versus obsolete outcomes.
@related media-loading.common.backend-failure, media-loading.common.completion-routing
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag ffprobe

@alias media-load = Cadroue.Media.LMediaLoad
@alias media = Cadroue.Media.LMedia
@alias custody = Cadroue.Core.LCustody

[backend-start] Backend load dispatch <input>
- Start the asynchronous backend media-load operation for the requested source @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> path-check

[path-check] Backend path normalization <decision>
- Normalize the requested source to a full path; invalid syntax enters LMediaLoadReject, which cancels prior ownership, advances generation, clears pending state, and builds an immediate failure @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media-load.LMediaLoadReject(...)
? "Path normalized" > request-owner
? "Invalid path syntax" > reject-raised

[request-owner] Backend request ownership <process>
- Cancel and dispose the previous request, create a linked cancellation source, advance generation, and mark the new request pending @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> source-check

[reject-raised] Invalid-path failure raised <process>
- Raise the immediate rejected outcome to each LMediaLoadCompleted subscriber individually, isolating subscriber exceptions @ media-load.LMediaLoadRaise(...)
> map:media-loading.common.completion-routing

[source-check] Backend source validation <decision>
- Require a nonblank path, an existing file, and a supported media extension @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media.LMediaCheck(...)
? "Supported existing media" > ffprobe-read
? "Blank, missing, or unsupported" > map:media-loading.common.backend-failure

[ffprobe-read] FFprobe media inspection <decision>
- Run the media reader off the caller thread; LMediaFfprobeRead launches ffprobe, attaches it to custody, kills its process tree on cancellation, parses JSON, and either returns LMediaInfo or throws @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media.LMediaFfprobeRead(...)
  @ media.LMediaFfprobeParse(...)
  @ custody.LCustodyAttach(...)
? "Parsed media returned" > completion-generation-check
? "OperationCanceledException" > cancelled-catch
? "Other reader exception" > map:media-loading.common.backend-failure

[completion-generation-check] Successful-read ownership check <decision>
- After a successful reader return, recheck disposal and generation; for a current request, distinguish a token that became cancelled from a successful media commit @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
? "Superseded or disposed" > obsolete-success
? "Current token cancelled" > cancelled-raised
? "Current parsed media" > success-commit

[cancelled-catch] Cancellation-exception ownership check <decision>
- On OperationCanceledException, first test disposal and generation before calling LMediaLoadFailCurrent; if still current, the failure helper performs its own second ownership check @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
? "Already obsolete" > obsolete-catch
? "Still current at first check" > map:media-loading.common.backend-failure

[obsolete-success] Successful reader became obsolete <output>
= LMediaLoadAsync returns LMediaLoadObsolete without raising LMediaLoadCompleted.

[cancelled-raised] Current token-cancelled outcome raised <process>
- Clear pending state, build the cancelled outcome, and raise it after leaving the backend lock @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media-load.LMediaLoadRaise(...)
> map:media-loading.common.completion-routing

[success-commit] Backend media commit <storage>
- Clear pending state, store current media path and parsed media information, and build the successful outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> success-raised

[obsolete-catch] Cancelled reader already obsolete <output>
= The caught cancellation returns LMediaLoadObsolete without raising LMediaLoadCompleted.

[success-raised] Successful backend outcome raised <process>
- Raise the successful outcome through isolated per-subscriber invocation @ media-load.LMediaLoadRaise(...)
> map:media-loading.common.completion-routing
